scuf-controller (2.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Move controller layouts out of the daemon into profile files under
    /usr/share/scuf-controller/profiles and /etc/scuf-controller.d. Adding a
    controller no longer needs a code change.
  * Match profiles by USB id, device name or capability signature, most
    specific first, so a profile written for one pad beats a generic layout
    that merely happens to fit.
  * Add --dump-profile to generate a starter profile from a connected pad,
    --list-profiles to show what is installed, and --profile-dir for testing
    a profile before installing it.
  * Allow axis overrides in /etc/scuf-controller.conf, alongside the existing
    button overrides.
  * Install via a distro-agnostic Makefile so the Debian packaging, the Arch
    PKGBUILD and the RPM spec share one set of paths. debian/rules now runs
    the profile checks at build time.

 -- Saieno <saieno86@gmail.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 20:15:00 -0500

scuf-controller (2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Replace xboxdrv with a self-contained python3-evdev daemon. xboxdrv was
    removed from Debian and Ubuntu during the Python 2 deprecation and last
    shipped in Ubuntu 24.04, so the old dependency could no longer be
    satisfied on any current release.
  * Grab the physical pad rather than deleting /dev/input/js0 from a
    per-minute root cron job. The grab stops duplicate input at the source,
    so the cron entry and its cleanup script are gone.
  * Modernise packaging: debhelper compat 13, drop the removed dh-systemd
    build dependency, declare ${misc:Depends}, add a Section field.
  * Run the service as Type=simple with Restart=always instead of a
    Type=forking unit around a backgrounded nohup, so systemd can track it.
  * Add /etc/scuf-controller.conf for device selection, profile choice,
    stick inversion and per-button overrides.
  * Add --list and --debug for identifying pads and checking the mapping.

 -- Saieno <saieno86@gmail.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 19:30:00 -0500

